**Summarizing project status**

I need to provide a concise final report. I'll mention that the full TypeScript (tsc) repository is failing due to unrelated issues. I want to reference the files that were changed and the related tests, using absolute file paths. It's worth noting that there are no changes in cache.ts because the invalidate function already existed. I should also mention the refresh operation via POST on the existing route and that the acceptance test is partly successful, despite the full tsc failing.
codex
Implemented the fix across approval, merge-readiness polling, and the review page.

Approval now invalidates merge-readiness cache when the request actually transitions to approved in [approve route](/Users/moltbot/pp-agent-work/factory-idea-027/src/app/api/v1/deploy-requests/[requestId]/approve/route.ts). The merge-readiness API in [merge-readiness route](/Users/moltbot/pp-agent-work/factory-idea-027/src/app/api/v1/deploy-requests/[requestId]/merge-readiness/route.ts) now retries 5 times with a 2s delay, and it also exposes a `POST` that invalidates the cached entry for manual refresh. In [review-page helpers](/Users/moltbot/pp-agent-work/factory-idea-027/src/app/pp/deploy-requests/[requestId]/review-page-helpers.tsx), `getBranchStatus()` now shows `Checks re-running after approval...` for approved requests when GitHub is still returning unknown/null mergeability.

On the UI side, [review page](/Users/moltbot/pp-agent-work/factory-idea-027/src/app/pp/deploy-requests/[requestId]/page.tsx) now tracks how long mergeability has stayed unknown and shows a `Refresh` button after 30s, which calls the new `POST /merge-readiness` endpoint and then re-fetches readiness.

Verification: `npx vitest run tests/deploy-request-tenant-safe-flow.test.ts tests/deploy-gate-approval-ledger.test.ts tests/review-page-helpers.test.ts` passed. I also ran `npx tsc --noEmit`; repo-wide typecheck still fails because of many pre-existing errors outside this bugfix, but a filtered pass over the changed files returned no errors.
